    "findings": [
      {
        "body": "Gain 4, Work 2, Harm 5\nRaise: Data loss\nCase: normal use - On a Linux host with `hidepid=ptraceable`, a process-access policy can prevent the SSH session from inspecting a still-running worker. Linux then hides its `/proc/<pid>` entry as well as preventing `ps` from reading it. The [kernel documentation](https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/proc.html) describes this visibility rule. The negated existence test treats the hidden entry as proof that the worker ended, so `--box off --yes` can delete its live worktree. The new test leaves the worker's `/proc` entry visible and therefore does not cover this case.",
